{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q412572","formula":"C₁₆H₃₀N₂O₃","hill":"C16H30N2O3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":16.0,"H":30.0,"N":2.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Piroctone olamine","ru":"Пироктон оламин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Piroctone olamine (INN; also known as piroctone ethanolamine) is an organic compound used as an antimicrobial active in anti-dandruff and anti-seborrhoeic dermatitis scalp products. It is the ethanolamine salt of piroctone, a hydroxamic acid derivative. It is described as a white to slightly yellowish-white crystalline powder with a mild characteristic odour, very slightly soluble in water and freely soluble in ethanol, chloroform, and ether.","ru":"Пироктон оламин (МНН: пироктоноэтаноламин) — представляет собой химическое соединение, используемое для лечения грибковых заболеваний. Является этаноламиновой солью, производным гидроксамовой кислоты. Впервые пироктон был синтезирован в 1979 году в Германии компанией Schwarzkopf-Henkel."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":44181993,"mass":298.42,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC(=O)N(C(=C1)CC(C)CC(C)(C)C)[O-].C(CO)[NH3+]","inchikey":"GHPFVSRTGHIHCD-UHFFFAOYSA-O","iupac":"2-hydroxyethylazanium;4-methyl-1-oxido-6-(2,4,4-trimethylpentyl)pyridin-2-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"44181993","atoms":51,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.457,"y":-3.935,"z":1.894,"el":"C"},{"x":2.508,"y":-2.467,"z":1.616,"el":"C"},{"x":3.412,"y":-1.649,"z":2.175,"el":"C"},{"x":3.436,"y":-0.189,"z":1.863,"el":"C"},{"x":4.324,"y":0.477,"z":2.398,"el":"O"},{"x":2.422,"y":0.224,"z":0.987,"el":"N"},{"x":1.465,"y":-0.608,"z":0.418,"el":"C"},{"x":1.525,"y":-1.926,"z":0.702,"el":"C"},{"x":0.412,"y":-0.092,"z":-0.556,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.968,"y":0.34,"z":0.02,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.834,"y":1.51,"z":1.0